Bundle-SymbolicName: io.nxmatic.rke2lab.seed.broker.codec
Export-Package: \
    io.nxmatic.rke2lab.seed.broker.codec
# Our OWN dual-realm library — the Document payload codec (DocumentCodec), which carries jackson.
# type=library is staged as a bundle (installed in-framework, importing the OSGi copy of jackson and
# the seed-broker seam) AND kept flat in the host uber-jar (binding the host copy) — jackson's own
# treatment, for our code. Its exported package legitimately lives in two realms: it is NOT a seam
# surface (no codec type crosses the String-only seed-broker seam; each realm holds its own copy
# bound to its own jackson), so DUPLICATE_REALM_CLASS exempts it like jackson. The .internal jackson
# glue (WireEnumModule) is NOT exported — only DocumentCodec is the API.
Provide-Capability: io.nxmatic.rke2lab.embed; type=library
# The jackson datatype modules DocumentCodec registers — jackson-datatype-jsr310 (JavaTimeModule,
# Instant) and jackson-datatype-jdk8 (Jdk8Module, Optional) — are IMPORTED bundle-to-bundle, exactly
# like jackson-databind — NOT nested. Both are genuine OSGi bundles; the staging closure stages each
# as a realm-library (this type=library imports its export) and keeps it flat host-side, so each realm
# binds its own copy. (Nesting is only needed when a ServiceLoader<Module> discovers the module off a
# classloader — as jsii's findAndRegisterModules does for jsr310 in manifests-cdk8s. We register
# modules EXPLICITLY, so there is no ServiceLoader and no nesting — even for jsr310 here.)
# JSpecify annotations are compile-only null-safety metadata (@NullMarked/@Nullable), yet
# RUNTIME-retained, so bnd would emit an Import-Package for org.jspecify.annotations — a package
# nothing resolves at runtime (no JSpecify bundle is staged in either realm). Drop it from the
# computed imports; the annotations do their job at compile/analysis time only.
Import-Package: !org.jspecify.annotations, *
-noimportjava: true
